    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "1. CONCEPT:\nBy the equation of continuity, $A_1 v_1 = A_2 v_2 \\implies v_2 = v_1 \\left(\\frac{r_1}{r_2}\\right)^2$.\n\n2. GIVEN:\n$r_1 = 4\\text{ cm}, r_2 = 2\\text{ cm}, v_1 = 1\\text{ m/s}$.\n\n3. FORMULA / PRINCIPLE:\nv_2 = v_1 \\left(\\frac{r_1}{r_2}\\right)^2\n\n4. STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:\n1. Ratio of radii: $\\frac{r_1}{r_2} = \\frac{4}{2} = 2$.\n2. Ratio of areas: $\\frac{A_1}{A_2} = 2^2 = 4$.\n3. Speed $v_2 = v_1 \\times 4 = 1 \\times 4 = 4\\text{ m/s}$.\n\n5. FINAL ANSWER:\nOption A: $4\\text{ m/s}$\n\n6. QUICK TIP:\nHalving the radius quadruples the velocity: $v \\propto 1/r^2$!",
